  "body": "Part of #1152 (and #290, D7). Found while working #1152.\n\n**What happens:** `electrode_from_faces` refuses a cavity when one of its walls is picked as a welded smooth face (`FeatureSel::Patch`): \"is a curved wall - an electrode is generated from planar walls only\". The same rounded corner picked as its planar strips yields a body electrode (#1152). A user who clicks a rounded corner can get the welded face, not the strips.\n\n**What is wanted:** `sinker_cavity::cavity_of` reads a welded wall when each of its facets is vertical and its bottom edge runs on the floor's ring. The cavity's outline is then the floor's ring as before, and the body electrode of #1152 burns it. A welded face with a facet that leans stays refused by name.\n\n**Evidence:** `crates/app/src/operation/sinker_faces.rs` (`face_of` returns a blank curved face for a patch), `crates/motion/src/sinker_cavity.rs` (`check_face`), `crates/app/tests/sinker_electrode.rs` (`a_rounded_pockets_corner_picked_as_its_welded_face_is_refused_by_name`).\n\n**Done means:** a rounded-corner pocket picked as its floor, four flat walls and four welded corner faces yields the same electrode as the pick of its planar strips, and the program verdict judges its burn clean. A welded face with a leaning facet is refused by name. Synthetic conditions only; state \"not exercised on a real EDM control\".\n\nLabels wanted (this account cannot set labels): `enhancement`, `P4`, `effort:high`, `area:3d`, `source:agent`.\n",
